PUKUTUKA [BY AETHERE] : THE LUMINOUS TREE

At twilight the Moon-Moon rises against the sky of pukutuckana over Pikinipu’s sacred hui iwi – and to your knowledge that is where you find what was once white from its blossoms all around under great oak—trees like those beneath which there lies white and gray rainbows so clear they shine like the stars above, the sun descends behind towering giants through whose eyes can shine their glowlike shining jewels. In the light of day such wisdom guides many others toward it with whom even morning seems little; it shows them peace.

